  "method": "Polylines read straight out of the PDF content stream (1 pt = 25.4/72 mm). The plan's outline is drawn as separate pieces plus a family of carve/binding lines, so the body silhouette is the outer boundary of all body lines rasterised at 1.5 px/pt, closed across the neck gap, opened morphologically to drop spurs, traced, smoothed and fitted with cubic Beziers (max 0.4 mm). Plan x/y rotated into app coordinates: X = (1842.75pt - planY) * k with treble +, Y = (1369.5pt - planX) * k. Origin: centreline, and the neck-pocket mouth which sits at the body/fingerboard junction.",
